From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sr-0w <Sr-0w@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 15:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hotdog: enable microphone routing

The SLIM Capture 1 back end already links SLIMBUS_0_TX to the WCD9340
AIF1_CAP port, and the codec node already carries micbias1 through
micbias4. No DAPM route connects an analogue microphone input to its bias
supply, so every ADC path stays powered down and the MultiMedia1 capture
front end has no reachable back end.

Restore the four analogue microphone routes. The bias assignment is the
one carried by the ClearStaff hotdog device tree this port is based on,
which pairs each input with the matching supply.

The OxygenOS odm mixer configuration confirms the resulting path is the
one the stock system uses: "handset-mic" resolves to "amic4", which
selects ADC4 through AMIC MUX0, routes DEC0 into CDC_IF TX0, and enables
AIF1_CAP Mixer SLIM TX0 on a single SLIM_0_TX channel. That is exactly
the back end already described above.

Note that sdm845-oneplus-fajita, the other upstream OnePlus board using
this codec, uses a different permutation (AMIC4 paired with MIC BIAS1).
The hotdog-specific tree is preferred here; if capture is silent, this
mapping is the first thing to re-test.

This change is capture-only. It adds no playback route and does not touch
the validated speaker path.

Signed-off-by: Sr-0w <Sr-0w@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
@@ -390,7 +390,11 @@
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	status = "okay";

-	audio-routing = "RX_BIAS", "MCLK";
+	audio-routing = "RX_BIAS", "MCLK",
+			"AMIC1", "MIC BIAS1",
+			"AMIC2", "MIC BIAS2",
+			"AMIC3", "MIC BIAS3",
+			"AMIC4", "MIC BIAS4";

 	mm1-dai-link {
 		link-name = "MultiMedia1";
--
2.50.1
